  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 960208,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10 Years 4 the Scene: A Commodore 64 Descent into Dystopia\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion in Oceania. But the Party’s grip remains absolute. In *10 Years 4 the Scene*, you play as a nameless citizen, struggling to survive in a London choked by surveillance and propaganda. This gritty, side-scrolling platformer for the Commodore 64 plunges you into a bleak world where individuality is a crime and Big Brother is always watching.\n\nNavigate treacherous environments – crumbling buildings, oppressive factories, and the ever-present telescreens – while evading the watchful eyes of the Thought Police. Collect scraps of forbidden knowledge and hidden messages to piece together the truth about the Party's continued control. \n\nGameplay focuses on precise platforming, stealth, and resource management.  Avoid detection, utilize limited tools to disable surveillance, and confront the psychological toll of living under constant scrutiny.  *10 Years 4 the Scene* isn't just a game; it's a chilling exploration of Orwell's vision, brought to life with the iconic limitations and charm of the Commodore 64. Can you resist the Party's influence, or will you become another cog in"
    },
